    "scope_check": "Strategist scope: supplying evidence to a peer seat and accepting its hold. No attempt to override the hold, and no re-assertion of the relayed authorization as sufficient -- the judgment is explicitly left with the seat holder. The standing-rule question is taken as pattern-shape to DRAFT; ratification remains the Director's. No merge, commit or push.",
    "applies_principles": [
      "bounded-authority -- a strategist may direct priorities within ratified shapes but may not lift a constraint the Director placed on a seat directly; the peer seat was right and is told so",
      "evidence-led -- the Director's instruction is quoted verbatim including its typo, with the message it answered, so the seat can judge the inference rather than trust the relay",
